   },
   "text": "Damage: RGB retains its three authored channels; the game computes weighted detail, premultiplied coverage, thermal glass and relief from these raw values. Alpha supplies the silhouette; values below 16/255 do not set the visible footprint. No sRGB conversion, invented PBR maps or generated replacement shape is involved. Default arithmetic is identity, followed by the reviewed nearest PNG8 storage boundary; exact RGBA export still requires the native comparison before publication. Contrast and bias edit raw detail; coverage scales original alpha without filling empty pixels. The preview uses ordinary material lighting for inspection only; Export writes the raw artwork. Keep the registered 256x256 pixel canvas and source coordinates. The native Export width/height fields retain that exact rectangle; no resizing helper is required."
  }
